# Never commit secrets or local state.
# NOTE: git ignore-rules do NOT support trailing inline comments - a '#' only
# starts a comment at the start of a line. Keep every pattern on its own line.
# your real values (token, domain, ssh key, issuer seed, Stripe keys)
terraform.tfvars
# ...and any hand-made copy of it. A promotion/rollback backup carries the same
# secrets as the original, and the bare name above would not have matched it.
terraform.tfvars.*
!terraform.tfvars.example
*.auto.tfvars
# downloaded provider binaries
.terraform/
# !! contains every resource attribute in plaintext, incl. the issuer seed + Stripe keys
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally NOT ignored - commit it. The
# dependency lock file pins provider versions/hashes so every apply resolves the
# same plugins (HashiCorp's recommended practice).
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
